IEEE 39-bus case data
---------------------

The included New England 39-bus test-system data are derived from MATPOWER
`case39`. The stable upstream source is
`https://github.com/MATPOWER/matpower/blob/b6c85b0323d20fb801cab3377c803a285d730847/data/case39.m`
in the `MATPOWER/matpower` repository, commit
`b6c85b0323d20fb801cab3377c803a285d730847`. The SHA-256 of the consulted
`data/case39.m` file is
`440833f998d1d8768c620477dacb6afd4e03f25f394bb0d200524513ad3fdc3c`.
It was consulted on 2026-11-18.

The numerical tables in `power_machine/cases/ieee39/case39.py` transcribe
only the case columns used by this project: bus number, `Pd`, `Qd`, area,
`Vm`, `Va`, generator values, branch values, and transformer ratio. The
coordinator compared the 39 buses, 10 generators, and 46 branches with that
source and found a maximum numerical difference of 0. `model.json` translates
those tables into this project's network schema and preserves source-row
mapping and source metadata. `dynamic_data.json` maps case identifiers, but
its dynamic machine parameters have separate provisional provenance.

The New England 39-bus system is a widely published and redistributed
academic test case. That description does not assert a license or a grant of
permission for the case data. The case is associated with the following
sources:

* T. Athay, R. Podmore, and S. Virmani, "A Practical Method for the Direct
  Analysis of Transient Stability," IEEE Transactions on Power Apparatus and
  Systems, 1979.
* G. W. Bills et al., *On-Line Stability Analysis Study*, RP90-1 report for
  the Edison Electric Institute, 1970.
* M. A. Pai, *Energy Function Analysis for Power System Stability*, 1989.
* R. D. Zimmerman, C. E. Murillo-Sanchez, and R. J. Thomas, "MATPOWER:
  Steady-State Operations, Planning, and Analysis Tools for Power Systems
  Research and Education," IEEE Transactions on Power Systems, 2011.

MATPOWER states that its case files are not covered by its BSD license. The
IEEE 39-bus case data in this repository are likewise not covered by this
repository's MIT License. No license for these data is asserted here. Their
use, redistribution, and modification require an independent review of the
provenance and applicable terms for the data.

The following files contain or transform data derived from MATPOWER `case39`:

* `power_machine/cases/ieee39/case39.py` contains the selected source columns.
* `power_machine/cases/ieee39/model.json` is the transformed network model.
* `power_machine/cases/ieee39/dynamic_data.json` maps the case generator and
  bus identifiers and records separate provenance for dynamic parameters.
* `power_machine/cases/ieee39/shortcircuit_data.json` contains explicit provisional sequence assumptions derived from the case network, without external reference results.
* `power_machine/cases/ieee39/LEEME.txt` documents those transformations and
  the local source hash.

